class:: OUProcess
summary:: Exact finite-step Ornstein–Uhlenbeck process
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>Processes
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Classes/BrownNoise, Classes/FBrownianMotion

description::

The Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process is a continuous-time stochastic process that modifies a standard random walk (Brownian motion) by adding a mean-reverting drift. Mathematically, the further the value drifts from the center, the stronger the rubber band pulls it back. Conceptually, this creates a perfectly smoothed, bounded, and continuous random signal. It acts as an ideal natural drift modulator for pitch (analogous to tape wow and flutter) or filter cutoffs, ensuring the value wanders organically without ever drifting infinitely out of range.

Generates the mean-reverting diffusion described by Ornstein and Uhlenbeck. Positive reversion uses the exact finite-time Gaussian transition; zero or negative reversion uses the Brownian limit.

Unlike link::Classes/BrownNoise::, OUProcess has explicit elapsed-time scaling, stationary mean/variance when reversion is positive, local deterministic seeding, and no hidden bounding.

subsection:: Process and stationary law

image::ou-process-dynamics.png#Left: an exact finite-step OU trace with mean = 0, reversion = 1, and diffusion = 1. Right: its stationary Gaussian density; the process fluctuates continually but is pulled back toward the center.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: mean
Long-run process mean.
argument:: reversion
Nonnegative pull toward the mean per model-time unit; negative becomes zero.
argument:: diffusion
Noise coefficient in state units per square-root model time.
argument:: timeScale
Model time per audio second; nonpositive values hold.
argument:: initial
State restored by reset.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local seed. Zero derives from the parent Synth.
argument:: reset
Restore initial state and original seed on a rising edge.
returns:: One audio-rate unbounded process state.

method:: kr
Control-rate version using the full control duration in the exact update.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ OUProcess.kr(reversion: 2).poll }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar(OUProcess.kr(600, 3, 180).clip(80, 4000), 0, 0.08) }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ Pan2.ar(PinkNoise.ar(0.08), OUProcess.kr(reversion: 1.5, diffusion: 0.8).tanh) }.play
)
::

code::
// Analog Tape Wow and Flutter
(
{
    var drift, freq, sig;
    // The mean-reverting drift of OU Process acts as a perfectly bounded random LFO
    drift = OUProcess.kr(reversion: 1.0, diffusion: 0.5);
    freq = 440 + (drift * 10);
    sig = Saw.ar(freq);
    Pan2.ar(RLPF.ar(sig, 2000, 0.3) * 0.2)
}.play;
)
::

code::
// Generative Drone Pitch Drifting
(
{
    var drift, freqs, sig;
    // Array of 4 OU processes, each wandering independently but always returning home
    drift = OUProcess.kr(reversion: 0.8, diffusion: 0.5 ! 4);
    freqs = [60, 64, 67, 71].midicps + (drift * 5); // Microtonal pitch bend
    sig = Splay.ar(Pulse.ar(freqs, LFNoise2.kr(0.2 ! 4).range(0.1, 0.5)));
    RLPF.ar(sig, 1200, 0.2) * 0.2
}.play;
)
::
